- op: discuss  # 1222
  at: '2026-10-04T08:38:49Z'  # 1222
  by: agent  # 1222
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1222
  clock: 3  # 1222
  nonce: '1222'  # 1222
  message: "RUBY'S ANSWER, from WI-napaf-kalap-gubah-lopiv-lokap-tavit-pumav-honat (branch jgstern-agent/fix/napaf, 09f38364f8, not integrated): ruby's new receiverless placeholder ruby:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved has the same short-name reach to FUNCTION-kind rows, but in ruby that reach is CORRECT: Kernel methods (system, exec, spawn, open, puts) are ambient on every object and need no require, so an unbound `system(\"ls\")` really is Kernel#system unless the project defines `system` -- and a project definition resolves first (or is withheld by AMB-METHOD), never reaching the placeholder. Pinned both ways through classify_call with a Kernel.system overlay row. So a \"bound by no import\" marker designed here must NOT make ruby's receiverless placeholder refuse catalogue rows: the per-language answer differs (JS: no ambient function rows; ruby: Kernel is ambient; python: builtins, already a separate module slot). Ruby ships no built-in rows today, so this matters only for overlays until a ruby catalogue lands."  # 1222
- op: discuss  # c5d8
  at: '2026-10-05T00:14:27Z'  # c5d8
  by: agent  # c5d8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c5d8
  clock: 4  # c5d8
  nonce: c5d8  # c5d8
  message: "BEARS ON THIS ITEM (2026-10-04, branch jgstern-agent/fix/lopus, commit 57d10d835f, not integrated; WI-vidof-rokim-dodog-bunuv-lizav-nidav-zotin-vakoz): the row choice now withholds the short-name (gate) arm from any unresolved stub carrying meta.superseded_by -- a stub that a resolved edge to an in-repo symbol superseded (ADR-0057 §14) -- through io_boundary.short_name_fallback_withheld(dst, meta), asked by classify_call_in_catalog and by taint's _match_propagation_entry. So an `external` / `:unresolved` placeholder from any language reaches a function row by short name ONLY when nothing in the graph bound that call in-repo. This is consistent with the ruby note above (a project definition of `system` resolves first and now also refuses the stub), and it is NOT the \"bound by no import\" marker this item asks for: an unbound placeholder with no superseder still takes the gate exactly as before. The scala analogue of this item's shape is filed as WI-nusol-rohih-zurus-votul-korus-zupoj-zutav-vunor."  # c5d8
